From 9cca4d48f92017d20f307023bfbd41e40d7a26b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shaun Adams <s.adams@f5.com>
Date: Tue, 16 Jun 2026 14:05:35 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] mt-handler-tenant-routing: provider/key handlers via dbStore
 + customer-FK tenant guard + isolation regression test
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Routes the legacy provider and provider-key admin handlers through the
tenant-scoped configstore so writes land via the GORM callback
(patch2) instead of the shared global in-memory map. Without this, two
tenants creating an "anthropic" provider race on the same map key and
the first one wins for every subsequent inference request.

* handlers/providers.go (addProvider):
  - Existence check goes through dbStore.GetProviderConfig (tenant-
    scoped via GORM callback) instead of the global c.Providers map.
    The legacy in-memory check 409'd cross-tenant collisions even
    though the DB carries composite (tenant_id, name) uniqueness.
  - DB write through dbStore.AddProvider, then best-effort in-memory
    sync so the still-shared inference runtime sees the new provider
    for this process lifetime. Stage 2 will replace the in-memory sync
    with a tenant-keyed map and drop the wart.
  - Rollback path uses dbStore.DeleteProvider with the request ctx
    (not context.Background()) so the DELETE flows the tenant_id
    through the GORM callback and can't wipe a sibling tenant's row.

* handlers/provider_keys.go: list / get / create / update / delete all
  route through dbStore (GetProviderKeys, GetProviderKey,
  CreateProviderKey, UpdateProviderKey, DeleteProviderKey). Each is
  tenant-scoped via the GORM callback. Best-effort in-memory sync
  after each write — same Stage 2 caveat.

* handlers/governance.go (createTeam / updateTeam): when the request
  sets customer_id to a non-empty value, validate the customer belongs
  to the calling tenant via h.configStore.GetCustomer (tenant-scoped).
  Without this a tenant could create a team whose FK points at
  another tenant's customer — a half-valid row the creator can't read
  back, and a potential information-leak vector.

* handlers/mt_governance_isolation_test.go (new): regression covering
  the two failure modes:
  1. Team-name uniqueness MUST be composite (tenant_id, name) — two
     tenants can both register a team called "engineering".
  2. customer_id MUST belong to the calling tenant — cross-tenant
     assignment is 400 with a specific message.

Scope note: BIFROST_ALLOW_PRIVATE_NETWORK env override + the
allowPrivateNetwork helper from mt-header are NOT carried here.
core.ValidateExternalURL at the OSS ancestor takes only a URL string
(no allow-private parameter), and the SSRF check site doesn't live in
the providers handler. The override can ship as a separate operator-
ergonomics patch when the upstream signature evolves.

Ref: https://jira.f5net.com/browse/XC-25496
